lls, can make correct decisions quickly. For D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner. Also \"considered moody\" and \"loner\". So we must use only those.\n\nWe need to produce a concise argument. Let's craft:\n\n\"I recommend Candidate A. A can anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, has excellent spatial vision, and very good leadership qualities \u2013 these support operational reliability, decision quality, technical competence, and crew cooperation. A is unfriendly, which may affect crew cooperation, but compared with B's pretentiousness and occasional wrong tone, C's communication difficulty and egocentric attitude, and D's moodiness and loner reputation, A's drawback seems less severe. Therefore A is the strongest overall fit.\"\n\nThat uses explicit facts. Good.\n\nNow metadata vote: Candidate A.\n\nProceed."}
